another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: \nL115:   1. 【61†Plonky3】\nL116:   2. 【62†Plonky3】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nmod.rs - source (https://docs.rs/p3-sumcheck/latest/src/p3_sumcheck/zk/mod.rs.html)\nciteturn2view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.rs/p3-sumcheck/latest/src/p3_sumcheck/zk/mod.rs.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 165\nL0: 【0†iframe】【1†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: ## Files\nL3: #\nL4: \nL5: p3_sumcheck/zk/\nL6: mod.rs\nL7: \nL8:     `【2†1】//! Honest-verifier zero-knowledge sumcheck for WHIR.\nL9:     【3†2】//!\nL10:     【4†3】//! Implements Construction 6.3 of eprint 2026/391 on top of both\nL11:     【5†4】//! stacked-binding modes — prefix and suffix.\nL12:     【6†5】//!\nL13:     【7†6】//! # Overview\nL14:     【8†7】//!\nL15:     【9†8】//! The plain WHIR sumcheck leaks the witness:\nL16:     【10†9】//! Each round polynomial coefficient is an affine function of the secret message.\nL17:     【11†10】//!\nL18:     【12†11】//! The HVZK variant blinds those coefficients with `k` small mask polynomials, one per sumcheck round.\nL19:     【13†12】//! Overhead: only `O(k * ell_zk)` extra field elements.\nL20:     【14†13】//!\nL21:     【15†14】//! # Protocol shape\nL22:     【16†15】//!\nL23:     【17†16】//! Let `k` be the folding factor and `ell_zk` the mask code message length.\nL24:     【18†17】//!\nL25:     【19†18】//! 1. Prover samples `k` univariate masks of degree `ell_zk - 1` over the extension field.\nL26:     【20†19】//! 2. The masks are batch encoded under a zero-knowledge code, MMCS-committed\nL27:     【21†20】//!    as one matrix, and absorbed into the Fiat-Shamir transcript.\nL28:     【22†21】//! 3. Prover sends `mu_tilde`, the sum of all mask evaluations over `{0,1}^k`.\nL29:     【23†22】//! 4. Verifier samples a combining challenge `eps` in the extension field.\nL30:     【24†23】//! 5. Per-round wire polynomial mixes:\nL31:     【25†24】//!    - the live mask,\nL32:     【26†25】//!    - past mask evaluations at sampled challenges,\nL33:     【27†26】//!    - future-mask endpoints,\nL34:     【28†27】//!    - the plain sumcheck contribution scaled by `eps`.\nL35:     【29†28】//!\nL36:     【30†29】//! # Round polynomial at a glance\nL37:     【31†30】//!\nL38:     【32†31】//! For round `j` with past challenges `gamma_1, ..., gamma_{j - 1}`:\nL39:     【33†32】//!\nL40:     【34†33】//! ```text\nL41:     【35†34】//!     h_j(X) = 2^{k - j}     * s_j(X)\nL42:     【36†35】//!            + 2^{k - j}     * sum_{l <  j} s_l(gamma_l)\nL43:     【37†36】//!            + 2^{k - j - 1} * sum_{l >  j} ( s_l(0) + s_l(1) )\nL44:     【38†37】//!            + eps           * plain_piece_j(X)\nL45:     【39†38】//! ```\nL46:     【40†39】//!\nL47:     【41†40】//! Verifier checks:\nL48:     【42†41】//!\nL49:     【43†42】//! ```text\nL50:     【44†43】//!     round 1  : h_1(0) + h_1(1) = eps * mu + mu_tilde\nL51:     【45†44】//!     round j>1: h_j(0) + h_j(1) = h_{j - 1}(gamma_{j - 1})\nL52:     【46†45】//! ```\nL53:     【47†46】//!\nL54:     【48†47】//! # Module layout\nL55:     【49†48】//!\nL56:     【50†49】//! - Proof record and mask oracle handle.\nL57:     【51†50】//! - Fiat-Shamir description of one masked batch, driven by every party.\nL58:     【52†51】//! - Prover-side sumcheck with mask sampling and round-polynomial assembly.\nL59:     【53†52】//! - Verifier-side replay with the dropped-coefficient reconstruction.\nL60:     【54†53】//! - Witness-free simulators, one per prelude, used to prove honest-verifier zero-knowledge.\nL61:     【55†54】//!\nL62:     【56†55】//! # Two preludes, and the scope of each\nL63:     【57†56】//!\nL64:     【58†57】//! A masked batch reaches its target one of two ways, and the description names which:\nL65:     【59†58】//!\nL66:     【60†59】//! ```text\nL67:     【61†60】//!     recorded claims  ->  the target is derived from the claims a verifier recorded\nL68:     【62†61】//!     inherited claim  ->  the target arrives as public input and is bound first\nL69:     【63†62】//! ```\nL70:     【64†63】//!\n"
